      "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c2_but_what_does_ccs_actually",
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "chunk_id": "s01_c02",
      "text": "But what does CCS actually optimize?",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.5806,
        0.5469,
        0.1444
      ],
      "target_source": "pptx"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 1,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c3_explains_its_target_derives_new",
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "chunk_id": "s01_c03",
      "text": "This paper explains its target and derives a new loss, Midpoint-Displacement, that matches CCS and can beat it.",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.75,
        0.5469,
        0.1111
      ],
      "target_source": "pptx"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 2,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c1_ccs_recovers_direction_activations_e",
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "chunk_id": "s02_c01",
      "text": "CCS recovers a direction in a model's activations encoding whether a statement is true or false, using no labels, only the constraint that a statement and its negation disagree.",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.2278,
        0.4466,
        0.6583
